-- CK-197: a refusal through a recursive payload says which payload. `H.eq`
-- is specialised to `Holder Int`, and `S`'s `SNode` holds `S (Holder a)`:
-- comparing that asks `S`'s own `==` at `Holder a`, and so the `eq` of
-- `Holder (Holder a)`, which `H.eq` never is — no `S` can be compared, and
-- `SLeaf 1 == SLeaf 1` is rightly NOT EQUATABLE. At 275b203 the message says
-- only "It holds a `Holder`, and comparing that needs the `eq` of `Holder`
-- at a type that `H.eq` does not have": neither the constructor nor the
-- payload. Expected: it names `SNode` and the type it holds.
pub type Holder a
    = Holder a


pub eq : Holder Int, Holder Int -> Bool
eq (Holder x) (Holder y) =
    modBy x 10 == modBy y 10
